  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Members may offer spare materials through an optional exchange shelf; every offer states the quantity and any conditions before acceptance.\", \"decision\": \"How should personally owned surplus materials be shared?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe steward collects labeled surplus offers for a weekly exchange period when owners and interested members can meet. A shared occasion concentrates handovers and allows questions about materials before recipients accept the stated conditions.\nOwners label surplus materials with their conditions and leave them on the exchange shelf for direct collection. Recipients can assess the offer independently, and the label preserves the owner’s terms during an unattended handover.\nOwners list surplus materials on the board and arrange a direct handover with the first member accepting the conditions. Materials remain with their owners until someone has committed to a specific and understood exchange."
    }
  ],
